## ✅ Fixed (committed `150d87d`)
1. **Tagline** → "OSIMIRI | **Luxury Redefined**" (was "Luxury Furniture Redefined").
2. **Search actually works now.** It was completely non-functional — the nav "Search" was a dead link to `/search?q=` with **no search box anywhere**, and it only searched static data. I rebuilt it: a real search field + live results from your **actual product catalogue** (plus collections & projects), each linking through. Verified: searching "sofa" returns the Aurelia sofa.
3. **Newsletter subscribe** — the footer button was **dead** (no handler at all). Now wired to save the email, with loading/success/error states.
4. **Forms fail gracefully** — instead of a raw 500 database error, they now show a friendly "email/WhatsApp us" message.

## 🔴 Critical gap found — your forms don't save (needs 1 SQL run)
**Every lead-capture form is broken** — I tested all 6 tables and they return 404: the enquiry popup, contact page, custom-furniture, architects, experience-centre appointments, **and** newsletter. The `schema.sql` (form tables) was never run in Supabase, so **nothing a customer submits is being saved.**

Fix: paste this into **Supabase → SQL Editor → Run** (same as you did for the catalog):

```sql
create extension if not exists pgcrypto;
create table if not exists general_enquiries (id uuid primary key default gen_random_uuid(), name text not null, phone text not null, email text, city text, requirement text, source_page text, created_at timestamptz default now());
create table if not exists custom_enquiries (id uuid primary key default gen_random_uuid(), name text not null, phone text not null, email text, city text, project_type text, brief text, created_at timestamptz default now());
create table if not exists architect_enquiries (id uuid primary key default gen_random_uuid(), name text not null, firm_name text, phone text not null, email text, city text, project_type text, project_scale text, created_at timestamptz default now());
create table if not exists contact_leads (id uuid primary key default gen_random_uuid(), name text not null, phone text not null, email text, city text, message text, created_at timestamptz default now());
create table if not exists experience_appointments (id uuid primary key default gen_random_uuid(), name text not null, phone text not null, email text, preferred_date date, time_slot text, message text, created_at timestamptz default now());
create table if not exists newsletter (id uuid primary key default gen_random_uuid(), email text unique not null, created_at timestamptz default now());
```

*(It's also in your repo at `supabase/schema.sql`.)* Once run, every form saves immediately — the code is already wired and uses the service-role key, so no policies are needed. **Or** send me the Supabase **database password** and I'll run it for you right now.

## 🟡 Minor gap noted
Footer **"Privacy Policy"** and **"Terms"** are plain text, not links (and the pages don't exist yet). Want me to add basic Privacy/Terms pages and link them?

All commits are local — push from GitHub Desktop. Want me to keep auditing (I can go page-by-page through Custom Furniture, Manufacturing, Architects, About for any remaining dead buttons or gaps)?

